## 8. Why is performance near chance? (checked)

`src/sanity_audit.py` found **no implementation problem**: labels and the positive-class column are aligned, every metric recomputes exactly with independent scikit-learn functions, shuffled-label controls give AUC {{sa_neg_range}}, and the same pipeline reaches validation AUC {{sa_pos_logreg}} / {{sa_pos_boost}} on a task that really has a difference. Cross-validation on train + validation ({{sa_cv_n_con}} continuum events, no test data) gives out-of-fold AUC {{sa_cv_logreg}} (logistic) and {{sa_cv_boost}} (boosting). **No physical separation is claimed.** Details: `reports/report.md`, section 5.

